Package: evca
Title: Expected Value of Eliminating Causal Ambiguity
Version: 0.4.0
Description: Computes the Expected Value of Eliminating Causal Ambiguity (EVCA),
    a decision-theoretic measure that quantifies the cost of acting under
    structural uncertainty about which causal model is correct. EVCA extends
    traditional value of information analysis (EVPI) from parameter uncertainty
    within an agreed model to between-model ambiguity: the situation where
    competing causal structures exist and no single one is accepted as correct.
    The package operates at the utility layer: it takes pre-computed expected
    utilities for each decision under each competing model and returns EVCA,
    exclusion costs (the welfare cost of omitting a model from deliberation),
    and Dirichlet sensitivity analysis over model weights. Upstream steps
    (causal model specification, parameter estimation, utility elicitation)
    are outside the current scope.
